          "lexical_rank": 1,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How much will my visit cost if I am paying out-of-pocket?\nAnswer: Out-of-pocket rates are $120 for a General Practitioner (GP) visit, $180 for a Dentist appointment, and $160 for all other specialist consultations.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 6,
          "similarity_score": 0.42419687,
          "dense_rank": 2,
          "lexical_score": 7.3636847,
          "lexical_rank": 2,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Copays and deductibles\n\nYour plan decides how much you pay at the visit. A copay is a fixed amount your plan sets for each visit, and it is collected when you check in. If your plan has a deductible you have not met yet, you pay the amount your plan allows for the visit at check-in. The front desk can estimate that amount for you if you give them your plan details before the visit.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 38,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.4173944,
          "dense_rank": 3,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## Medical procedures\n\n- 93000: resting 12-lead electrocardiogram, with the doctor's reading of it - $65\n- 94010: spirometry - $85\n- 93784: 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure monitoring - $140\n- 81002: urine dipstick test done in the clinic - $15\n- 69210: ear wax removal, per ear - $75\n- 17110: wart freezing (cryotherapy), up to 14 warts in one session - $90",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 38,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.39030665,
          "dense_rank": 4,
          "lexical_score": 2.5540674,
          "lexical_rank": 5,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n\nYour itemized receipt lists each procedure done at your visit by its billing code. Medical procedures use five-digit CPT codes, and dental procedures use CDT codes that start with the letter D. If you pay out of pocket, each procedure below is charged at the price shown, in addition to the rate for the visit at which it is done.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 38,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.3846842,
          "dense_rank": 5,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## Dental procedures\n\n- D2391: tooth-coloured filling on one surface of a back tooth - $210\n- D2140: silver (amalgam) filling on one surface - $160\n- D7140: simple tooth extraction - $240",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 32,
